# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) for local development.
#
# Production values are set in the Vercel dashboard, not here — see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.

# ── Browser-facing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The origin the BROWSER uses for API calls (src/lib/api/client.ts).
#
# Local:      http://localhost:8080  — the browser talks to salary-service directly.
# Production: leave it EMPTY. An empty value makes every request relative (`/api/...`), which the
#             rewrite in next.config.ts proxies to the backend. That is what keeps the SameSite=Lax
#             session cookie working across two hosts — see that file's comment for why.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# ── Server-only ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute backend origin, used by the Next.js server: the rewrite destination (next.config.ts) and
# the server-side identity read (src/lib/auth/current-user.ts). Never exposed to the browser.
#
# Local:      unset — current-user.ts falls back to NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL.
# Production: https://<your-service>.onrender.com
# API_ORIGIN=
